    "biography": "<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.oQ2AhEeDkwdPRv71]{Profile: Liam O'Connor}</p><blockquote><p><em>“I wore this badge before there was a port. They took it from me with three photos.”</em></p></blockquote><table class=\"sbn-ficha\"><tbody><tr><th>Epithet</th><td>The Sheriff That Was</td></tr><tr><th>Concept</th><td>Witness and informant (A2-E04)</td></tr><tr><th>Clan</th><td>Brujah</td></tr><tr><th>Sect</th><td>independent</td></tr><tr><th>Sire</th><td>A union Brujah, destroyed in 1934</td></tr><tr><th>Born</th><td>1868</td></tr><tr><th>Embraced</th><td>1899</td></tr><tr><th>Ambition</th><td>For the truth about 1978 to be on the record.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Demeanor</h3><p>Looks about thirty-one. Huge and round-shouldered, red hair and a short beard, a broken nose and cauliflower ears; undershirt, suspenders, and a wool cap.</p>",
    "appearance": "<p>Looks about thirty-one. Huge and round-shouldered, red hair and a short beard, a broken nose and cauliflower ears; undershirt, suspenders, and a wool cap.</p>",
    "equipment": "<ul><li>DOC-08: the original letter, kept in a plastic sleeve under the ring</li></ul>",
    "notes": "",
    "privatenotes": "<p>Editor&#39;s Note: doc 07 said “looks about fifty” and “graying red hair”; his age at the Embrace was settled on instead (about 31, red hair with no gray).</p>",
